import React from "react";

export function EvidenceCodeContent() {
  return (
    <div className="lawyer-code-content criminal-code-content font-merriweather space-y-3">
      <div className="flex justify-center mb-6">
        <img src="/Legislation/DOJ Logo.png" alt="DOJ Logo" className="h-48 w-auto object-contain" />
      </div>
      <h1 className="text-[28px] font-bold text-center mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather uppercase tracking-wide">CODE OF EVIDENCE AND JUDICIAL PROCEDURE</h1>
      <p className="text-[16px] font-normal text-center mb-8 text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0] italic font-merriweather">(EVIDENCE CODE)</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]">THE CODE OF EVIDENCE AND INVESTIGATION LAW (Evidence Code)</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 1. General Provisions and Principles of Evidence Law</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.1</span>Code of Evidence and Investigation Law.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.1.1</span>This Code of Evidence and Investigation Law establishes the Principles of Evidence and the forms that Evidence may take as well as the laws and regulations required in order to obtain such Evidence through investigations and to use that Evidence in order for Law Enforcement Officers, Judges and Lawyers to reach a decision or Verdict during a Hearing or Trial.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.2</span>Rules and Principles of the Code of Evidence and Investigation Law.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.2.1</span>This Code of Evidence and Investigation Law is promulgated in order to establish provisions and regulations over Investigations, the gathering of Evidence and the presentation of that Evidence to a Law Enforcement Officer, Judge or Lawyer and the forms and validity of any Evidence that may be used under the law.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>In the event of a conflict or a need for clarification between provisions of this Code and any other State Law, or a conflict of provisions within this Code itself, the Supreme Court shall make an Official Judicial Ruling as to the provisions that apply and the order of primacy of those provisions.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.2.2</span>Any Amendments to the Law by the Government, the Congress of the State or Judicial Rulings made by the Supreme Court shall not apply retroactively and will only have force of law from the date of promulgation or publication.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.3</span>Rules and Principles of Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.3.1</span>Evidence is defined as a body of information that may be used within the law to establish the facts of an Investigation and establish the Proof of any Claims made to the Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.3.2</span>Proof of a Claim (eg: Charges against a Suspect or Claim for loss or damages) is provided through Evidence that is both Valid and Admissible.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any Evidence submitted must be Probative meaning that it must tend to prove the relevant facts of the Case.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Any Evidence that is irrelevant or does not tend to prove facts that are important to the Case may be Excluded from consideration by the Court under the Exclusion Rule.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any arguments or additional statement(s) may only be based on the Admissible Evidence and should be both reasonable and logical.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Any assumptions and speculations based on the Evidence or insufficient Evidence to support any speculation may not be made.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Any arguments cannot be based on hearsay or guesswork that is not supported by the Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.3.3</span>Where any Evidence is determined to be Invalid or Inadmissible, that Evidence may not be considered by the Court and is to be excluded from any considerations of the Court under the Exclusion Rule.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.3.4</span>Where the relevancy of any Evidence presented is to be contested in Court a Lawyer may raise an Objection to the Relevancy of the Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A Judge may make a Ruling as to the Relevance of the Evidence or may request that the reason for the Evidence being submitted or the line of questioning of a Witness be clarified.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.4</span>Rules and Principles of the Burden of Proof in an Investigation.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.4.1</span>The Burden of Proof for any actions taken against a Citizen of the State during an Investigation, including the Detention of a Suspect for Identification, Questioning and possible Search of the Citizen, lies with the Law Enforcement Officer(s) who are conducting the Investigation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.4.2</span>Any actions during an Investigation without sufficient Valid Evidence to prove those actions were reasonable and lawful, or where specific actions were required but were not done either through negligence or omission of action by the Law Enforcement Officer(s), must be considered by the Court in the context of the situation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A Judge may make a Ruling as to the effect on the Investigation (eg: Unlawful Detention and Search) and the outcomes on any further legal action based on the conduct of the Law Enforcement Officers involved.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.5</span>Rules and Principles for the Gathering and Recording of Evidence by State Employees.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.5.1</span>All State Employees must ensure that they have a valid Proof of Bodycam (eg: turns on Bodycam) and that their Bodycam is working and ready to record at all times while On-Duty.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.5.2</span>All State Employees must have a valid Bodycam Recording of all Major Incidents they were involved in while On-Duty. This includes:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>All State Employees present at the scene of a Detention and/or Arrest are required to record the full Detention and/or Arrest.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Recording of any Detention and/or Arrest must be complete and include the Identity of the Suspect and any Evidence for why the Suspect was Detained and/or Arrested, any Search of the Suspect, and the full duration of while the Suspect was in Custody.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>All State Employees present during any Use of Lethal Force against a Citizen of the State are required to record the Situation (as per the Firearms Code).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>All State Employees present at a Global or Emergency Situation in the State must have a valid Bodycam Recording of the Situation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.5.3</span>State Employees are not required to have a Recording of any ordinary duties or performance of public services (eg: Selling of Gun Licences or Vehicle Insurance) but must be ready to start Recording in the event of a Major Incident or any escalation of a situation.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.6</span>Rules and Principles for the Retaining of Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.6.1</span>All Law Enforcement Officers and Civil Servants must retain all Evidence of any Major Incident for a minimum of 48-hours from the time of the Incident.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.6.2</span>Where any Evidence has been formally requested by a Judge or Lawyer for a Case File or a Subpoena for that Evidence has been issued by the Court, that Evidence must be provided before the 48-hour period has ended.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any Bodycam Evidence that has been formally requested must also be retained for at least 7-days from the time of Recording unless clear instruction is given by the Court that the Evidence is no longer required.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.6.3</span>Where this Evidence cannot be provided, or is otherwise not available or is later made unavailable by the State Employee, the Court may impose Criminal and/or Civil Liability on the State Employee whose duty it was to retain or provide that Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.7</span>Rules and Principles for the Chain of Custody of Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.7.1</span>The Chain of Custody of Evidence is a Principle that requires any Evidence to have valid Proof as to how the Evidence was obtained and made available for use and/or presentation during an Investigation, Case or Trial.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any possession or knowledge of any Evidence by a Party to the Case must be logical or a valid Proof of the Chain of Custody of Evidence must be available to indicate how the Evidence was obtained from another Party.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>This may include a Handover for any relevant Evidence that is to be used to start an Investigation, Case File or Warrant (eg: a Handover of an SSD card for Bodycam Evidence).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Where a Law Enforcement Officer or other Witness is present and is able to present Evidence directly to a Judge or Lawyer, no Handover of Bodycam Evidence is required (eg: during a Hearing with a Lawyer).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Where a Law Enforcement Officer or other Witness is not physically present, no presentation of their Evidence is permitted unless a prior Handover of that Evidence has been done and Proof of the Chain of Custody of Evidence is available.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>A Handover of any Legal Documentation (eg: a Warrant or Case File) includes a Handover of all Evidence included in the Documentation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.7.2</span>Where the Chain of Custody of Evidence is in doubt a Lawyer that is Party to the Case or Trial may raise an Objection to the Chain of Custody of the Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Judge must make a Ruling as to whether the Evidence was reasonably available for use and/or presentation in the Investigation, Case or Trial.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.8</span>Rules and Principles for a Request for Evidence by a Judge or Lawyer.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.8.1</span>A Judge has a Right to Order a Law Enforcement Officer to report to the Capitol Courtroom to present Evidence that is required for a Hearing, Trial or Appeal.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>In order for the request to be made, sufficient Valid Evidence must be available prima facie to justify the request (eg: clear proof from the PDA that the Law Enforcement Officer was the Arresting Officer or clear identification on a Bodycam Recording that has been presented).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>This Order may be given on the Department Radio and if the Law Enforcement Officer is not available, their State Organisation must reply to this effect and should notify the Judge when the Law Enforcement Officer will be available if that information can be provided.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A Subpoena for the Bodycam Evidence must be issued and handed to a High Command from the Law Enforcement Officer’s State Organisation if a direct presentation of the Evidence is not possible at the time of the request.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.8.2</span>A Lawyer has a right to ask for Evidence regarding any Case they are Party to and this request may not be denied unless there are lawful grounds for denying access to that Evidence (eg: Classified Evidence).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Access to basic Evidence about their Client such as their Wanted Status, Criminal Record and any Charges and/or Fines must be provided to a Lawyer by a Law Enforcement Officer or the Government (GOV) immediately on request and cannot be denied.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A Lawyer must be able to prove that they have a Contract with their Client in order to make the request.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>This includes Proof of the Charges or any Penalties and Fines that have been imposed on their Client following a Case File, Trial or Hearing that has been concluded.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">iii)</span>If requested, this Evidence must immediately be provided by the Law Enforcement Officer(s) who Processed their Client or the Law Enforcement Officer’s State Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Where a Lawyer has been denied or not provided with any requested Evidence they may approach the Department of Justice (DOJ) for further actions under the law and/or the issue of a Subpoena for that Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.8.3</span>A High Command of a State Organisation has the right to request Bodycam Evidence from an Employee of their State Organisation if the request is made as part of their reasonably expected duties to their State Organisation or is defined as part of their duties in the Charter of the State Organisation (eg: an Internal Affairs or Legal Department).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.9</span>Rules and Principles of Anonymous Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.9.1</span>Where necessary, as determined by the Attorney General or a Judge, or following a petition to the Court by a Witness or their Lawyer, the identity of a Witness may be considered Anonymous and the origins of the Evidence and the Identity of the Witness will not be publicly available and must be kept secret.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>If required, only the Attorney General and the Judge(s) will be party to the Evidence and will review the Evidence privately.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any Lawyer who is Party to the Case and requires knowledge of that Evidence may only be permitted to review the Evidence by the permission of the Attorney General or the Judge(s) and only under a special non-disclosure agreement regarding the identity of the Witness.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.9.2</span>Where testimony, interview or cross examination is required for a Witness to provide Anonymous Evidence, this testimony shall be conducted outside of the open Court Proceedings (often referred to in law as in camera “in private”) in order to protect the Identity and thus the safety of the Witness.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Where necessary for Direct Examination or Cross-Examination in Court, the questions, and their answers, will be relayed between the Witness and the Court by the Judge, or shall be submitted between the Witness and the Court in writing.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.10</span>Rules and Principles of Classified Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.10.1</span>Classified Evidence is any form of Evidence or Information where public knowledge of that Evidence shall unduly harm the State or the conduct of Special Operations by State Organisations.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Evidence or Information that is Classified may not be revealed or discussed with any State Employee unless it is essential for that State Employee to be aware of the Evidence or Information in order to perform their Duties to the State.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Evidence or Information that is Classified may not be revealed or discussed with a Civilian.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.10.2</span>The purpose of Classification is to limit access to that Evidence and/or Information in the interests of the State and State Security.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Evidence may not be declared Classified in any way that is arbitrary or without a valid reason.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Evidence may not be declared Classified in such a way that excludes the Governor.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>Evidence may not be declared Classified in such a way that excludes the Attorney General from performing their Duties to the Justice System of the State (eg: First Person Immunity Case).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>Evidence may not be declared Classified in such a way that excludes a Supreme Court Judge who is presiding over a Case or Trial.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">e)</span>Evidence may not be declared Classified in such a way used to exclude the Leader of a State Organisation or Head of a Department of the Government (GOV) from that Evidence where it is required to be known in order for them to perform their expected Duties to the State (eg: the Head of Homeland Security or the Director of the United States Secret Service).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.11</span>Rules and Principles of a State’s Witness.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.11.1</span>If Valid Evidence can be provided by a Suspect who wishes to turn State’s Witness, the Attorney General or a Supreme Court Judge may, in exchange for the provision of such Evidence, offer the Suspect:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>An Exemption from Criminal Prosecution.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>An Exemption from Civil Liability.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>A Commutation or Reduction of Sentence or other Penalties.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.11.2</span>The Evidence shall be evaluated under Client-Attorney Privilege by the Attorney General or a Supreme Court Judge who shall determine the validity and weight of such evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The validity and content of this evidence must be considered and must be found to be both material and relevant to a further Investigation of a greater crime or a greater threat to the State than any crimes committed by the State’s Witness before any Exemption from Prosecution or Commutation may be offered.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.11.3</span>The Evidence from the State’s Witness may be considered Anonymous Evidence on application to a Supreme Court Judge if it is determined to be necessary for the protection of the Witness or the Witness requests protection of their Identity.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.11.4</span>The Evidence from the State’s Witness may further be considered Classified Evidence on application to a Supreme Court Judge if it is determined to be necessary under the circumstances and based on the nature of the Evidence provided.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.12</span>Rules and Principles for the Duration of Validity for Video and Photo Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.12.1</span>All Photograph and/or Video Evidence from a Bodycam Recording remains valid for 7-days from the time of the Recording of the Evidence unless directly specified in the law that the Evidence remains valid for a longer period of time (eg: Bodycam Recordings for a Bar Examination).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>If a Case or Court Trial cannot be concluded with this Evidence then the Case must be dismissed without a Verdict on the Grounds of an Unreasonable Delay of Justice and on the Grounds of Expired Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">1.12.2</span>The Court may impose Criminal or Civil Liability on any Party to the Case that intentionally causes an Unreasonable Delay of Justice or where their inaction or unavailability to appear in Court causes any relevant or significant Evidence to Expire.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Where necessary to prevent the Expiry of Evidence, the Court shall hold a Trial in absentia as per the provisions of the Lawyers Code.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 2. Definitions in Evidence Law</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.1</span>Definition of an Investigation.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.1.1</span>An Investigation is defined as any actions or measures taken by a Law Enforcement Officer in order to clarify the circumstances, nature and relevant facts associated with an offence and the gathering of this Evidence for presentation to the Court or in a Case File.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.2</span>Definition of Reasonable Suspicion.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.2.1</span>Reasonable Suspicion is defined as the legal standard required in order to conduct a limited Procedural Action against a Citizen of the State, in the form of a Detention or a brief Search as a Stop and Frisk (also referred to as a Terry Stop).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A Suspect may only be Searched under Reasonable Suspicion if the Law Enforcement Officer has seen the Suspect is in possession of any Firearms or if there is a clear and reasonable suspicion that the Suspect was involved in a crime.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.3</span>Definition of Probable Cause.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.3.1</span>Probable Cause is defined as the legal standard required in order to conduct Procedural Actions against a Citizen of the State, including a Detention and/or Arrest and a Search of that Citizen or their Property or Vehicle.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Probable Cause requires that, at the moment of the Detention and/or Arrest, or before a Search of the Citizen, the State Employee has reasonably trustworthy information or facts supported by Valid Evidence that the Suspect had committed an offence or was committing an offence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Hearsay and other forms of Unreliable Evidence or Testimony cannot be regarded as Probable Cause.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Probable Cause cannot be determined to have been correct after-the-fact (eg: if the Law Enforcement Officer did not have any Probable Cause but the Search of the Suspect then proved the Probable Cause for the Search).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.4</span>Definition of a Witness.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.4.1</span>The term Witness refers to all persons who were present at a situation or crime scene and may provide Evidence or Witness Statements as to the situation. This includes:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Arresting Officer(s).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any other Law Enforcement Officer(s) who were present at the situation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>Any Citizen of the State who may be involved in the situation or crime scene, including possible Accomplices and any Unwilling Participants.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>Any other Witnesses or Bystanders who witnessed the situation but were otherwise not involved in the commission of any crime(s).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.5</span>Definition of Admissible Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.5.1</span>Admissible Evidence is defined as any Evidence that may be used within the law to prove the facts of an Investigation, Case or Trial.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.5.2</span>In order for any Evidence to be considered Admissible Evidence:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>It must be Valid Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>It must be Probative Evidence in that it must be considered relevant to proving the facts of the Case.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>It must be lawfully obtained and logical in the manner in which the Evidence is used in the Case.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.6</span>Definition of Valid Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.6.1</span>Valid Evidence includes all Evidence that can be used to establish the facts of an Investigation or Case.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>In order for Evidence to be considered Valid Evidence it must meet any reasonable requirements to be Valid (eg: turns on bodycam).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.6.2</span>Valid Evidence may still be considered Inadmissible Evidence if it does not meet the other criteria given under the provisions for Admissible Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.7</span>Definition of Invalid Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.7.1</span>Invalid Evidence is defined as any Evidence whose validity cannot be reasonably established under the requirements and provisions for Valid Evidence (eg no Proof of Bodycam).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.7.2</span>All Invalid Evidence is also considered Inadmissible Evidence and is to be regarded as Excluded Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.8</span>Definition of Inadmissible Evidence</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.8.1</span>Inadmissible Evidence is defined as any Evidence that cannot be considered Admissible Evidence and therefore cannot be used during an Investigation or is later determined to be obtained without compliance with the necessary standards and procedures to be considered Admissible Evidence during a Hearing or Trial.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.9</span>Definition of Illegal Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.9.1</span>Illegal Evidence as a general term is defined as all Evidence that has been obtained by a violation of the Rights of a Citizen (eg: a violation of privacy) or was only obtained by committing a crime or other direct violation of the law against the Suspect (eg: Robbing a person then finding they have an Illegal Firearm).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.9.2</span>Where it is determined that Evidence against a Suspect was obtained illegally, a Judge must consider how the Evidence was obtained and the circumstances by which the Citizen, Law Enforcement Officer(s) and/or Civil Servant(s) came by that Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Where the actions taken to obtain the Evidence are a clear violation of the law with criminal intent, Criminal Liability may be imposed on the parties responsible.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Where there is no criminal intent or the Illegal Evidence was obtained by Law Enforcement Officers acting in good faith that their actions were lawful, the Court may recommend Disciplinary Sanction or further training be given to the Officers.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.10</span>Definition of Supporting Evidence</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.10.1</span>Supporting Evidence includes all Valid and Admissible Evidence that does not necessarily prove the facts of the Case but may be logically used to support other Valid Evidence presented (eg: Blood Marks do not indicate who was shot at a location but it does clearly indicate that someone was shot or injured at that location).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.11</span>Definition of Excluded Evidence (The Exclusion Rule).</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.11.1</span>Excluded Evidence is defined as any Evidence that must be excluded from the considerations of the Court and any Judge(s) or Lawyers as well as all Law Enforcement Officers that are involved in the Investigation, Case or Trial.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">2.11.2</span>The Exclusion Rule of Evidence requires that only the Evidence that is both Valid and Admissible may be considered for an Investigation, Case or Trial.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any Inadmissible Evidence must be Excluded from any considerations by the Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any Invalid Evidence, as well as information or subsequent evidence that has been obtained using Invalid Evidence as its basis must be Excluded from any considerations by the Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>Any Illegal Evidence, as well as information or subsequent evidence that has been obtained using Illegal Evidence as its basis must be Excluded from any considerations by the Court (this is referred to as the Fruit of the Poisoned Tree).</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 3. Standards of Evidence in the Law</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.1</span>Rules and Principles of the Standards of Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.1.1</span>The Standards of Evidence act as guidelines for Law Enforcement Officers, Judges and Lawyers to determine the strength and relevance of Evidence against a Suspect or the Accused in an Investigation, Case or Trial.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.1.2</span>These Standards of Evidence are presented in order from the lowest standard to the highest standard.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.2</span>No Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.2.1</span>Under the Standards of Evidence, only those Charges or Claims that have some form of Valid Evidence may be considered by the Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Where No Evidence can be presented, or the Evidence presented is determined to be Invalid, Illegal or Inadmissible and no other Valid Evidence can be presented for any Claims or Charges, the Case must be dismissed by the Court due to No Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.3</span>Insufficient Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.3.1</span>Under the Standards of Evidence, where the Evidence is Incomplete or there is Insufficient Evidence to prove any Claims or Charges, a Ruling or Verdict cannot be made by the Court and the Case must be dismissed under the Presumption of Innocence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.4</span>Circumstantial Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.4.1</span>Under the Standards of Evidence, where there is Valid Evidence that may indicate a violation of the law at the scene of the crime but no clear identity of the Suspect or the commission of a crime by the Suspect cannot be proved to have taken place that Evidence is considered circumstantial and inferences or assumptions may have been made based on these circumstances (eg: A Suspect was at or near an ATM Robbery but there is no Evidence that they were involved in the ATM Robbery).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Where the Evidence presented is determined to be purely circumstantial and no other Valid Evidence can be presented that would directly prove any Claims or Charges, the Case must be dismissed by the Court under the Presumption of Innocence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.5</span>Prima Facie Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.5.1</span>Under the Standards of Evidence, Evidence Prima Facie (“at first sight&quot; or &quot;at first look.&quot;) does not assert that the Evidence is sufficient for a Verdict or that all the Claims made are true however it does assert that, given the Evidence already presented, further Investigation and gathering of Evidence should be authorised as there are some clear facts that have been established (eg: the Name and State Organisation of the Arresting Officer using the PDA).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Prima Facie Evidence is the minimum standard for which the Department of Justice (DOJ) may request the Bodycam Recording of a Law Enforcement Officer for any Appeal or Complaint made by a Citizen against that Law Enforcement Officer.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.6</span>Preponderance of the Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.6.1</span>Under the Standards of Evidence where there is a Preponderance of the Evidence there is no single part of the Valid Evidence that could lead to a Verdict, however, when the weight of all Evidence is taken into account, a limited Verdict in a Civil Case can be reached as the Claim(s) may be considered likely to be true.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A Preponderance of the Evidence cannot be used to prove the Charges in a Criminal Case.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.7</span>Clear and Convincing Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.7.1</span>Under the standard of Clear and Convincing Evidence, the Evidence presented indicated that the Claim(s) made in a Civil Case are more likely to be true than false and that the Court may make a Civil Verdict on the strong belief that the Claims made are a fact.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Clear and Convincing Evidence is still considered insufficient to be used to prove the Charges in a Criminal Case.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.8</span>Evidence Beyond a Reasonable Doubt.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">3.8.1</span>Beyond a Reasonable Doubt is the highest Standard of Evidence and any Charges against a Suspect or Claims made to the Court have been established and any doubts as to the facts of the Case would be considered unreasonable.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Where the Evidence for any Claims or Charges is Beyond a Reasonable Doubt, the Court may make a full and clear decision as to the Case.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 4. Rules for Valid Evidence</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.1</span>Forms of Valid and Admissible Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.1.1</span>The following Forms of Evidence within this Article are only a guide to assist Judges, Lawyers and Law Enforcement Officers determine what Evidence may be used for an Investigation and/or Case and any requirements for that Evidence to be Admissible as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>This is not a full list of all the possible Forms of Evidence and any Evidence that is relevant and probative to a Case may also be used so long as it is logical in its application and can be proved to be reasonably known.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.2</span>Bodycam Evidence and Recording for State Employees.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.2.1</span>In order for any Bodycam Evidence to be Valid and Admissible it must comply with the following provisions:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A Valid Bodycam Proof. Any Bodycam Recording must have a Valid Proof which must show that the Bodycam was turned on and is recording (this is also referred to as the Proof of Bodycam).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>There is no set format for a Proof of Bodycam and a Bodycam Recording will be held as Valid so long as it is reasonable from the Proof of Bodycam to understand that a Bodycam was being used.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Arbitrary arguments or objections as to what constitutes a Valid Proof of Bodycam may not be made (eg: arguing what different coloured lights mean on a Bodycam).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">iii)</span>The Proof of Bodycam must clearly show the Date and Time when the Bodycam was turned on and there may not be any obstructions to the Date and Time.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">iv)</span>The Proof of Bodycam must be valid for that day or shift (a Proof of Bodycam resets after 4am and a new Proof of Bodycam must be done for the new day).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">v)</span>If a State Employee changes their Clothing or Uniform (for any reason) they must do a new Bodycam Proof while in the new Clothing or Uniform.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">vi)</span>Any small changes in accessories (eg: a change in tie, glasses or gloves) or changes to headwear or body armour do not count as a change of Clothing and do not invalidate any existing Bodycam Proof.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">vii)</span>A State Employee being sent to the Hospital does not make a Proof of Bodycam Invalid (but does invalidate the Bodycam Recording itself as per the below provisions).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>A Valid Bodycam Recording. The Bodycam Recording is the video footage from the Bodycam and order to be Valid, a Bodycam Recording must not violate the provisions of Article 5 (Invalid Evidence) and must also comply with the below rules:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Evidence from a Bodycam Recording may not be used if the Recording clearly shows the State Employee was sent to the Hospital during or at the end of the situation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>The Evidence from a Bodycam Recording may not be used if the Bodycam was Broken or Destroyed during the situation. A Bodycam can be inspected to confirm whether it is broken or damaged to confirm this as a fact.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">iii)</span>There is no requirement for a Refresh or Restart of a Bodycam Recording (eg: following a return from a Code A) or directly at the start of any Bodycam Recording as the start of the Bodycam Recording is self-evident and may be used as Evidence so long as there is a valid Proof of Bodycam.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.2.2</span>Any additional requirements for Special Bodycam Evidence (eg: for an FIB Raid Warrant) must be clearly defined in the Charter of the Federal Investigation Bureau (FIB) and its Training Manuals but only applies to that State Organisation’s activities when gathering Evidence for a Raid Warrant and may not be imposed over any State Law to other State Organisations or the Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.2.3</span>Any Bodycam Proof and Bodycam Recordings only apply while the State Employee is On-Duty and any Proof of Bodycam or Recording of Bodycam as a State Employee may not be used while Off-Duty.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The State Employee must use a Personal Bodycam as per the below regulations for Citizens while Off-Duty.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.3</span>Bodycam Evidence and Recording for Citizens.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.3.1</span>A Civilian or Off-Duty State Employee may use a Personal Bodycam or purchase and use a GoPro Bodycam from a 24/7 Store and use it to provide Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Personal Bodycam must be able to be proved as valid (Proof of Bodycam) otherwise it cannot be used as evidence under law.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A GoPro purchased from a 24/7 clearly indicates while it is recording and this is considered a Valid Proof that a Bodycam was being used to Record.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Any use of a Personal Bodycam must comply with the standards for a Proof of Bodycam as given in 4.2 (above) and has the same limitations for the Evidence from a Bodycam Recording being used as Valid Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.4</span>Document and Records Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.4.1</span>All Document Evidence does not expire unless a Duration, or a Date and Time of Expiry are clearly indicated on the Document itself (eg: The Martial Law Act) and all Official Documents shall otherwise remain valid so long as the Document and the Proof of Signing the Document can be provided.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.4.2</span>Any Official Registry and any entry on an Official Registry or Records of the Government of the State (GOV) that are required for the keeping of important Records for the State do not expire or the Records themselves have a clear duration for how long they are valid for (eg: the Payment of Business Taxes for a set period of time). This includes, but is not limited to:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Registry of Licensed Lawyers of the State.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>The Registry of Tax Payments and Businesses of the State.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>The Financial Records of the Government and all Financial Audits of State Organisations.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.4.3</span>All Official Documents for the State must be Signed by the appropriate State Authorities and Parties to the Document before the Document has legal force.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>In order for any Legal Documents (including Case Files, Orders, Warrants) to be considered Valid, the Document must be Signed by the Lawyer and an appropriate Judicial Authority (eg: the Attorney General or a Judge) as detailed in the Lawyers Code.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>In order for a Contract to be considered Valid, the Contract must be Signed by the Party or Parties to the Contract.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A Contract of Employment and Agreement with the Provisions of the State Organisation’s Charter needs to only be Signed by the Employee.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>The Charter of a State Organisation must be Approved and then Signed by the appropriate State Authorities (State Organisation Leader, Governor and Attorney General) in order to be considered valid.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.4.4</span>The Signatures of all Parties to the Signing of any Official Documents must be included in the Document as the Proof of Signature.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.5</span>Photographic (Photo) Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.5.1</span>Photo evidence is only valid if the Date and Time of the Photo is visible, or clearly identifiable on the Photo and the violation is likewise clearly identifiable.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Photo Evidence lacks context and is considered a weak form of Evidence in most cases (except Traffic or Parking Violations) but can be used as Supporting Evidence in an Investigation or Case.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Where a Traffic Fine or Penalty is issued to a Vehicle, the Licence Plate must be clearly visible on the Photograph and the relevant Traffic Violation must also be visible on the Photograph (as per the Traffic Code).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.6</span>Search Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.6.1</span>A Search of a Suspect or Vehicle may be used as Evidence if the Search was Valid according to the law and/or the Grounds for the Search of a Suspect.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.6.2</span>Any Direct Evidence or Physical Evidence from a Valid Search of a Suspect or Vehicle that establishes a clear and reasonable connection with the crime being committed at a crime scene may also be used as Evidence (eg: the Suspect has a Keyset at the scene of an ATM Robbery).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.7</span>Crime Scene Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.7.1</span>Evidence from a Crime Scene such as Blood Traces, Footprints and Tire Marks may be used as Supporting Evidence during an Investigation.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.8</span>Ballistics and Firearms Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.8.1</span>Ballistics Evidence includes Any Firearms or Ammunition that have been dropped by a Suspect and are clearly visible on Bodycam.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A Law Enforcement Officer is permitted to collect this Evidence but only if it is safe to do so (may not collect during an ongoing dangerous situation such as a gunfight) and may retain this Evidence for presentation to a Judge or Lawyer as per the Provisions of the Firearms Code.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>The Law Enforcement Officer must dispose of the Evidence in the correct manner at their Headquarters as soon as it is no longer needed as Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.9</span>Witness Statements and Testimony (Verbal and Written).</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.9.1</span>Eye-Witness Statements or Other Testimony (including additional Testimony by a Party that can be considered relevant to the Case) that has been given Under Oath or has been stated by the Suspect following the Reading of the Miranda Rights may be used as Evidence for an Investigation, Pre-Trial Hearing or during a Trial in Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.9.2</span>During an Investigation, Testimony can take the following forms:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Affidavit. An Affidavit is Testimony that is given in writing Under Oath during an Investigation or outside of Court Proceedings.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Affidavit must be signed and handed to the Lawyer or a Judge and Proof of Signature and Chain of Custody of the Affidavit must be included with the Affidavit.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>As the Affidavit is given in written form, the Oath must be available on the Affidavit Document presented to the person Under Oath.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Deposition. A Deposition is Testimony that is given verbally Under Oath during an Investigation or outside of the Court Proceedings.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Deposition must be Recorded by the Lawyer or a Judge and Proof of Bodycam and the Evidence given during the Deposition must be clear on the Recording.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.9.3</span>During a Trial in Court, Witness Testimony can take the following forms:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Direct Examination. Direct Examination is the process of asking questions to a Witness who has been called to provide testimony by one side (eg Prosecution or Defence) during a Trial in Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Cross Examination. Cross Examination is the process of asking questions to a Witness who has been called to provide Testimony by the opposing side (eg: the Defence asking question of a Witness called by the Prosecution) during a Trial in Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.9.4</span>In all instances of a Witness presenting Testimony as Evidence they shall be advised that such Testimony is being given Under Oath and the Witness must be read the Oath as follows: “Do you [insert name] hereby swear and affirm that the contents of your statement are true to the best of your knowledge, as well as accurate to the best of your abilities and that the consequences for false statements are severe and may entail monetary Fines and Imprisonment.”</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.9.5</span>In order for any Testimony to be upheld, the Witness must agree to be bound by the above Oath before any Testimony is given and a full Recording must be taken of the Testimony given.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Proof of Bodycam as well as Proof of Saving the Bodycam as Evidence must be retained and included with the Testimony.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Where necessary a Chain of Custody of the Testimony must also be provided if a Party to the Case is to use the Testimony as Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.10</span>Statements by a Suspect During Detention and/or Arrest.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.10.1</span>Any Statements (including a Confession) by a Suspect or the Questioning of a Suspect after they have been Detained and/or Arrested may only be permitted to be used as Evidence if the Suspect has clearly been read their Miranda Rights and acknowledged that they understand their Rights.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>If a Suspect has not been read their Miranda Rights which advises the Suspect as to their Right to Remain Silent (which is based on the Right to Not Self-Incriminate), then any Statements made or Answers to questions by Law Enforcement Officers are Inadmissible as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>If a Suspect has requested a Lawyer then no Questioning of the Suspect is permitted during the Detention and/or until their Lawyer has arrived and been permitted to speak to the Suspect.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.11</span>Organisation Internal Log (Leaderboard) Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.11.1</span>Records or Logs of events from a State Organisation’s Logs (such as Taking and Returning of State Organisation Firearms, Ammunition and Equipment or the Promotion or Dismissal of an Employee) may be used as Evidence or as Supporting Evidence to establish any facts or a sequence of events for an Investigation.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.12</span>PDA Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.12.1</span>Personal Digital Assistant (PDA) evidence must be able to be proved as Valid (Proof of PDA Connection) otherwise it cannot be used as evidence under law.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.12.2</span>Only those facts from the PDA that can be reasonably and logically known may be used as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Previous Fines may not be used as Evidence of any previous crimes committed unless there is also a matching entry on the Previous Crimes.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>PDA Evidence is considered sufficient Evidence prima facie for a Subpoena of the Arresting Officers Bodycam in the event of an Appeal of a Criminal Conviction.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.12.3</span>A Background Check on the PDA for State Employment should confirm that the Employee does not have:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any Prior Prison Terms.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any Association with Criminal Elements (may not have been Seen in Criminal Structures).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>Any Previously Committed Crimes (including any past Wanted Status).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.13</span>Organisation eMail.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.13.1</span>Only those eMail Channels (eg: Employee’s Logs or Announcement Channels) that are reasonable to be considered Valid Evidence may be used as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>All other eMail (including Chat Channels, Private eMail or Direct Messages sent via eMail) that are not considered valid communications may not be used as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Official State Channels on the Government email are considered to be Valid Evidence as these Channels are necessary to facilitate communication between the State Organisations and the Government (GOV), including notifications about State Employees who have been added to the State Blacklist.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.14</span>GPS Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.14.1</span>Evidence from an alert through the PDA or any GPS coordinates sent via a Phone for a Reported Crime or Medical Emergency may be used as Supporting Evidence as to the time and location of a possible crime or reported crime as well as provide the Identity of the Citizen who reported the crime.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.15</span>VIN Evidence and Vehicle Licence Plates.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.15.1</span>The Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) Number and Owners Details of a Vehicle may be used as Evidence only if an inspection of the VIN number and further vehicle information can be proved.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>If no Licence Plate is visible on a Vehicle or the Licence Plate is missing, a check of the VIN Number and Owners Details must be used as Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.16</span>Phone Evidence (Calls and Messages).</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.16.1</span>Any Phone Calls that are clearly heard and recorded on Valid Bodycam may be used as evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Name of the owner of the Phone Number (using an immediate PDA search of the Phone Number) must be established Beyond a Reasonable Doubt in order for any action to be taken against them.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.16.2</span>Any Phone Messages Sent or Received may be used as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Names of the owners of the Phone Number(s) the messages are sent to, or from, must be established Beyond a Reasonable Doubt (using an immediate PDA search of the Phone Number) in order for any action to be taken against them.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.17</span>Radio Communications.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.17.1</span>Written and/or Verbal Communications on an Organisation Radio, Department Radio, Club Chat or Family Chat can be used as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Radio Communications are not themselves necessarily a crime (unless the content of the communication is clearly stated as a crime in the Criminal Code) as while it may indicate possible criminal intent, further proof that a crime was committed is required (eg: under the Principle of Corpus Delicti) unless the Radio Communication is itself a crime.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Radio Communications may be considered as Evidence for Civil Cases (including Labour Law Cases) and Civil Liability or Disciplinary Sanction may be imposed based on this Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.18</span>Identification of a State Employee and Citizens.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.18.1</span>As a general rule, if the Citizen can recognise another Citizen by name then they are able to clearly and legally identify the Citizen and this will be held as valid Evidence and Proof of Identity.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.18.2</span>A Citizen can be identified in this manner (including while wearing a Mask or other face covering Clothing or Accessories).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Employees of a State Organisation are able to recognise any other Employees of the same State Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Employees of a Private Organisation are able to recognise any other Employees of the same Private Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>Members of the same Family are able to recognise any other Members of the same Family.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.18.3</span>While a State Employee is wearing a Mask, Citizens are able to recognise the State Employee if they have seen the State Employees Passport or their Badge/ID.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.18.4</span>While a Citizen is wearing a Mask, other Citizens are able to recognise that Citizen if they have seen the Citizens Passport.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">4.18.5</span>While a Citizen is wearing a Mask, a Law Enforcement Officer is able to recognise that Citizen if they have checked the Citizens pockets for their Personal Details.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 5. Rules for Invalid Evidence</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.1</span>Rules for Invalid Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.1.1</span>The following Forms of Evidence within this Article are written as a guide to assist Judges, Lawyers and Law Enforcement Officers determine what Evidence is considered Invalid and therefore may not be used for an Investigation and/or Case and to give clear examples of these.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>This is not a full list of all the possible Forms of Invalid and Inadmissible Evidence and any other determinations as to the Validity and/or Admissibility of Evidence shall be determined by Attorney General, a Judge or the Court.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.2</span>Corrupted Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.2.1</span>Corrupted Evidence includes any low-quality Photograph or Bodycam Recording, in which important objects and subjects are hardly distinguishable or severely distorted, as well as any Bodycam Recording, where the sound is not heard at all or severely distorted during any significant portion of the Recording is considered Invalid and Inadmissible as Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.3</span>Manipulated Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.3.1</span>Any Photograph or Bodycam Recording that has been edited, doctored or otherwise altered in an attempt to misrepresent the situation or conceal part of the Bodycam Recording is considered Manipulated Evidence and is considered Invalid and Inadmissible as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Edits can be made to highlight a point (red circles, crops, etc.) however complete unedited Evidence should always be available of the same.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Small Icons, Bodycam Branding or Personal Markings on a video are not considered Manipulated Evidence so long as the full screen is visible and the overlays do not permanently hide any significant Evidence or necessary details (such as the Date and Time).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.3.2</span>Any Submission or Presentation to the Court of any Manipulated Evidence with the intent to misrepresent a situation shall be considered a crime.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.4</span>Incomplete Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.4.1</span>Any Incomplete Photograph or Bodycam Recordings where footage of the full situation cannot be provided may be considered Invalid and/or Inadmissible as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any Bodycam Recordings should be free from breaks and cuts and the Recording should be continuous during any situation (eg: during the Detention and/or Arrest of a Suspect).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>A short changeover or refresh where the Bodycam is Saved and immediately restarted is not considered Incomplete Evidence so long as no significant Evidence is missing or another Bodycam Recording can be provided that shows the situation during that break in the Bodycam.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>Whether the photo or video evidence is Incomplete or not is decided by the Judge after evaluating the Bodycam Recording(s) and hearing the circumstances from both sides.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.4.2</span>Any Photograph or Bodycam Recordings as well as any Proof that a Bodycam was being used but where the Date and Time are not visible shall be considered Incomplete Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.5</span>Missing Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.5.1</span>Any Evidence that, when required to be presented or submitted to the Court, is found to be missing, either in part or in whole is considered Missing Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Citizen who is responsible for the retaining or presentation of the Evidence may be held liable for any loss or destruction of that Evidence once the fact of the situation and reasons for the Missing Evidence are established.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.6</span>Unreliable Testimony.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.6.1</span>Any Testimony of the Victim of a Crime or any Witness that is based on guesswork, assumption, hearsay or the Verbal or Written Testimony of a Witness who cannot indicate the source of their knowledge or where there is no reason to believe they were present at a situation or crime scene, may be considered Unreliable Testimony and is considered Invalid and Inadmissible Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.7</span>Private eMail.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.7.1</span>Private eMail or direct messages sent via eMail may not be used as Evidence under any circumstances.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>All communications that are to be used as Evidence must be undertaken in a form that is recognised as Valid Evidence (eg: in person or through a phone or the official channels in an eMail).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.8</span>Second Hand Recordings.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">5.8.1</span>Any Audio, Photograph or Bodycam Recordings that are done so “second hand” through an eMail or other sources is considered Invalid and Inadmissible as Evidence and cannot be used under any circumstances.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any Bodycam Recording must be directly recorded by the Citizen who is presenting the Evidence or must otherwise be handed over on an SSD to the Citizen who will be presenting the Evidence (such as a Law Enforcement Officer or Lawyer) in accordance with the Chain of Custody of Evidence.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 6. Rules for Illegal Evidence.</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.1</span>Forms of Illegal Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.1.1</span>The following Forms of Evidence within this Article are written as a guide to assist Judges, Lawyers and Law Enforcement Officers determine what is considered Illegal Evidence and thus may not be used for an Investigation and/or Case and may result in Criminal Charges if it is determined that a crime was committed in gathering or creating this form of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>This is not a full list of all the possible Forms of Illegal Evidence and any determinations as to the Validity and/or Admissibility of Evidence shall be determined by the Court.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.2</span>Illegally Gathered Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.2.1</span>Illegally Gathered Evidence includes all Evidence that has been obtained by a direct violation of the law (eg: a Search in direct violation of a Citizens Rights) or was only obtained by committing a crime against the Citizen (eg: Robbing a person then finding they have an Illegal Firearm then reporting them for possession of Illegal Firearms).</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.3</span>Fabricated Evidence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.3.1</span>Any Evidence that is staged or fabricated or where the Suspect was framed through the planting of Evidence (eg: handing them Drugs or Illegal Firearms) is to be considered Fabricated Evidence and is both Illegal Evidence and Inadmissible Evidence against the Suspect and will result in Criminal Liability for the Citizen that fabricated or planted the Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.4</span>Violation(s) of Attorney-Client Privilege.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.4.1</span>Any Evidence that has been submitted where the provisions of Attorney-Client Privilege have been violated by a Third Party who is not covered under the Contract between the Lawyer and their Client or the related Provisions for Joint Defence or Common Cause between Lawyers and their Clients shall be considered Illegal Evidence.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.5</span>Violation(s) of Privacy.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.5.1</span>Violations of the Privacy of a Citizen without a valid reason or no Probable Cause may be considered as Illegal Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>This includes any unlawful access to Private Property without any lawful Grounds to enter the Property or without the permission of the Owner of that Property in order to gather Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>This includes violations of Doctor-Patient Confidentiality (eg: while a Suspect is receiving Medical Treatment at a Hospital or at the DOC).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>This includes any unlawful sharing of personal information (Properties Owned, Phone Number or Criminal Record) unless that information is being used for a lawful investigation or for legitimate reasons (eg: a requested Background Check on the Department Radio).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">6.5.2</span>The Citizen who has violated the privacy of another Citizen in an unlawful manner may be held criminally liable for violations of privacy or the unlawful disclosure of private or confidential information.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 7. Laws and Procedures for the Search of a Citizen</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">7.1</span>Rules and Principles for a Search of a Suspect or Citizen.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">7.1.1</span>Law Enforcement Officer(s) or Civil Servant must have a clear and valid reason under the law in order to conduct a Search of any Citizen of the State.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Law Enforcement Officer must document the Search showing the items that were found on the Suspect.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Where a Search of a Citizen is valid, all Illegal Items must be Confiscated immediately.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>A State Employee may not act in any manner to force other Grounds for the Search to be valid (eg: they may not move the Suspect to the Capitol to then force a Search by USSS based on the fact that the Suspect is now on Capitol Grounds).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>Where a Suspect is contesting the validity of the Detention, Arrest or Search by immediately requesting a Lawyer, no Search or Confiscation is permitted until the validity of any Procedural Actions (eg: Detention, Arrest and/or the Search) against the Suspect have been proved.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>If a Suspect delays their request for a Lawyer, the Law Enforcement Officer cannot be held liable for any Confiscation that is later found to be unlawful or invalid.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">e)</span>Where a Search of a Citizen is not valid, no Confiscation of any Illegal Items or Property is permitted unless the Citizen is to be Processed into the Department of Corrections (DOC) on other Grounds (eg: is Wanted by the State) or has committed further crimes after their initial Detention and/or Arrest (eg: Attempted to Escape or Failure to Comply).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">7.1.2</span>A Citizen of the State or a Suspect may be subjected to a Search by Law Enforcement Officers and/or Civil Servants only on the following Grounds:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>On the Grounds of Consent. A Citizen may be Searched if they have clearly consented to the Search and the grounds for the Search are reasonable.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A Citizen has the right to refuse to give Consent if they believe there are no reasonable Grounds for the Search.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Refusal to give consent to a Search cannot be considered a Failure to Comply or Grounds for further Investigation unless other valid Grounds for the Search apply.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>On the Grounds of Reasonable Suspicion. A Suspect may only be Searched under Reasonable Suspicion if the Law Enforcement Officer has seen the Suspect is in possession of any Firearms or if there is a clear suspicion that the Suspect was involved in a crime (eg was seen leaving a crime scene).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Where any Suspicion is considered unreasonable or the Search is determined to be without any clear and valid reasons, any Search of the Suspect shall be considered Inadmissible Evidence and no Charges may be imposed based on the unlawful Search of the Suspect.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>On the Grounds of Probable Cause. Probable Cause requires that, at the moment of the Detention and/or Arrest, or before a Search of the Citizen, the State Employee has reasonably trustworthy information or facts supported by valid Evidence that the Suspect had committed a crime or was currently committing a crime.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Probable Cause cannot be proved to have been correct after-the-fact (eg: if the Law Enforcement Officer did not have any Probable Cause but the Search of the Suspect then proved the Probable Cause for the Search).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Where the Law Enforcement Officer(s) cannot prove any Probable Cause for the Search, any Search of the Suspect shall be considered Inadmissible Evidence and no Charges may be imposed based on the unlawful Search of the Suspect.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>On the Grounds of a Valid Arrest. A Suspect may be Searched during a valid Arrest or if they are currently Wanted by the State.and all Illegal Items must be Confiscated immediately before transporting them to the Department of Corrections (DOC) for Processing.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Where the Law Enforcement Officer(s) cannot prove the Arrest was valid, any Search of the Suspect shall be considered Inadmissible Evidence and no Charges may be imposed based on the unlawful Search of the Suspect.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">e)</span>On the Grounds of Martial Law. When Martial Law is in effect in the State of San Andreas, any Citizen may be Searched according to the Provisions of the Martial Law Act.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">f)</span>On the Grounds of Capitol Security. The Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and the United States Secret Service (USSS) Agents have special authority to conduct a Search of any Citizen or near the Capitol Grounds for security reasons.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Capitol Grounds are defined as the Capitol Building itself (including any Garages) as well as the block around the Capitol, including all streets and sidewalks on both sides of the road.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">g)</span>On the Grounds of Protective Security. The United States Secret Service (USSS) Agents have special authority to conduct a Search of any Citizen of the State who is in the vicinity of any First Person of the State who is formally under USSS protection.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">h)</span>On the Grounds of Military Security. The National Guard (NG) has the authority to conduct a Search of a Citizen if that Citizen is present at Fort Zancudo (FZ) or wishes to enter Fort Zancudo (FZ).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>In addition, the National Guard Military Police (NGMP) have the authority to conduct a Search of any National Guard Soldier and their Personal Vehicle while at Fort Zancudo (FZ).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>On the Grounds of Correctional Security. Department of Corrections (DOC) Officers have full authority to conduct a Search of any Law Enforcement Officer, Civil Servant or Citizen of the State present at the Department of Corrections (DOC). This provision includes:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Any Prisoner currently serving a term of Imprisonment at the State Prison.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Any Law Enforcement Officer or Civil Servant who is currently at the State Prison and is not there to Process a Suspect into the DOC.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">iii)</span>Any Citizen who is requesting Entry (a Tour) or Visitation with a Prisoner who is currently serving a term of Imprisonment at the State Prison.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">j)</span>On the Grounds of Judicial Security. The Bailiffs of the Court as well as the Attorney General or a Judge have full authority to conduct a Search of any Citizen present in the Capitol Courtroom to ensure the safety of all Parties to the Court Proceedings.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">k)</span>On the Grounds of an Unwilling Participant. An Unwilling Participant in any criminal activity may be Searched as part of the Investigation in order to establish whether they were possibly involved in the crime or are otherwise an accomplice to the crime.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">l)</span>On the Grounds of a Warrant. A Citizen or their Property may be searched where a Warrant of Search (Search Warrant) of that Suspect or their Property has been signed by the Attorney General or a Judge.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 8. Laws and Procedures for the Search of Private Property</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">8.1</span>Rules and Principles for a Lawful Search of a Private Property or Residence.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">8.1.1</span>Law Enforcement Officer(s) must have a clear and valid reason under the law in order to enter and conduct a Search of any Private Building or Residence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Law Enforcement Officers must announce their presence as soon as they enter the Private Property and state the reason for the entry.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>If a Citizen claims they are the Owner of the Property or claims they are a member of the Family that owns the Property, they may be checked on the PDA for proof that they are the Owner of the Private Property or a member of the Family.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>If a Citizen is discovered to be the Owner of the Property or is lawfully present in the Property (eg: a Family Member at a Family House) then they may not be Searched and must be Released immediately unless there are valid Grounds for the Search (eg: the Suspect is Wanted by the State) or they clearly are the Suspect being chased.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>If the Owner of the Property is present, Law Enforcement Officers should leave as soon as it is confirmed that the Suspect is no longer inside the Private Property and the Owner requests the Law Enforcement Officers to leave their Private Property.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">8.1.2</span>To enter or conduct a Search of a Building or Residence, Law Enforcement Officers must have one of the following Grounds:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>On the Grounds of Consent by the Owner. A Private Property or Residence may be Searched only if the Owner of the Private Property or Residence is present and has granted permission to access the Property and conduct the Search.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A Citizen has the right to refuse to give Consent if they believe there are no reasonable Grounds for the Search.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Refusal to give consent to a Search cannot be considered a Failure to Comply or Grounds for further Investigation unless other valid Grounds for the Search apply.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>On the Grounds of Probable Cause. Where a Private or Family Residence is the scene of a crime (eg: a House Robbery) or a reported disturbance then Law Enforcement Officers may enter Private Property to Investigate.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Owner of the Property and their Vehicles may not be Detained or Searched on their Private Property without a Search Warrant or unless the Owner is clearly identified as the Suspect.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>On the Grounds of the Pursuit of a Suspect. If a Suspect has clearly fled into a Private Property during a pursuit by a Law Enforcement Officer and the search is urgent, a Search can be carried out by Law Enforcement Officers without a Warrant and without the Consent of the Owner.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>On the Grounds of a Warrant of Search (Search Warrant). A Private Property or Residence may be Searched if a Warrant of Search, signed by the Attorney General or a Judge, has been issued for that Property.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Warrant may only be executed once and the Department of Justice (DOJ) must be notified that the Search has been conducted.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">8.1.3</span>The Law Enforcement Officer(s) and/or Civil Servants must record the whole procedure of any Search of Private Property and retain the Evidence for 48-hours.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 9. Laws and Procedures for the Search of a Vehicle</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">9.1</span>Rules and Principles for a Lawful Search of a Private Vehicle.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">9.1.1</span>Law Enforcement Officer(s) must have a clear and valid reason under the law in order to conduct a Search of any Vehicle.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Law Enforcement Officer must retain valid Evidence of the reason for the Search and the conduct of the Search for a minimum of 48-hours.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>The Law Enforcement Officer must reasonably have access to the Trunk of a Vehicle in order to conduct a Search by allowing the Driver or Owner to open the Trunk or by breaking the Trunk open (only if the Driver is not present).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Any Search of a Vehicle where it is unreasonable for the Law Enforcement Officer(s) to have access to the Trunk shall be considered Inadmissible Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">9.1.2</span>To conduct a lawful Search of a Vehicle, Law Enforcement Officers must have one of the following Grounds:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>On the Grounds of Consent by the Owner. A Vehicle may be Searched only if the Driver or the Owner of the Vehicle is present and has granted permission to conduct the Search of the Vehicle.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A Citizen has the right to refuse to give Consent if they believe there are no reasonable Grounds for the Search.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Refusal to give consent to a Search cannot be considered a Failure to Comply or Grounds for further Investigation unless other valid Grounds for the Search apply.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>On the Grounds of Probable Cause. If there is Probable Cause to Arrest the Driver of the Vehicle and they have used the Vehicle in the commission of a crime, or has likely stored Evidence of the crime in the Vehicle, the Vehicle may be Searched as part of the Investigation to gather additional Evidence against the Suspect.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>A Search of a Vehicle is not permitted during a Traffic Stop where the Driver has only committed a Traffic Violation (eg: the Law Enforcement Officer is only issuing a Speeding Fine).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Where the Law Enforcement Officer(s) cannot prove any Probable Cause for the Search of the Vehicle, any Search of the Vehicle shall be considered Inadmissible Evidence and no Charges may be imposed based on the unlawful Search of the Suspect’s Vehicle.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>On the Grounds of Martial Law. Where Martial Law is in effect in the State of San Andreas, any Vehicle may be Searched according to the Provisions of the Martial Law Act.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>On the Grounds of a Search Warrant. A Vehicle may be Searched if a Search Warrant of that Vehicle has been Signed by the Attorney General or a Judge.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>The Warrant of Search must clearly indicate the Name of the Owner, Licence Plate Number and Type of Vehicle.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Only the Vehicle detailed in the Warrant of Search may be Searched and only if the Ownership, Licence Plate and Vehicle Type match to the details on the Warrant.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">e)</span>On the Grounds of a Raid Warrant. Any Vehicles may be Searched if they are present at the location for a Raid by State Organisations as detailed in an approved Raid Warrant.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">f)</span>On the Grounds of a Vehicle Impound. Where a Vehicle is to be Impounded, Law Enforcement Officers have the right to Search the Vehicle in order to inventory the Vehicle and its contents for Impound.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">9.2</span>Rules and Principles for Confiscation of Illegal Items from a Vehicle.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">9.2.1</span>A Law Enforcement Officer may Confiscate all Prohibited and/or Illegal Items from a Vehicle only if there are valid Grounds for the Search.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Law Enforcement Officer(s) must be able to prove they have access to the Trunk of a Vehicle (eg: breaking the trunk) in order to Search a Vehicle and conduct a Confiscation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any Search and Confiscation from a Vehicle where it is unreasonable for the Law Enforcement Officer to have access to the Trunk or the Search itself is unlawful shall be considered an Unlawful Search and Seizure.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>All Law Enforcement Officers are required to store Evidence of the Search and Seizure from the Vehicle for at least 48-hours.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">9.2.2</span>If a Confiscation is unlawful, then the Law Enforcement Officer(s) may be held liable for any loss of lawfully owned Property to the Suspect in the event of unlawful Confiscation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Illegal Firearms, Prohibited Items or any other Illegal Items as defined by the State and/or the Criminal Code may not be considered lawfully owned Property.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather">Article 10. Conduct of a State Inspection by the Government.</h2>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.1</span>Rules and Principles for a State Inspection.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.1.1</span>A State Inspection is an Investigation conducted by the Government of the State (GOV) to ensure compliance by a State Organisation and the Employees of that State Organisation with the laws, standards and regulations of the State.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A State Inspection should be conducted on each State Organisation at least once per week.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>A State Inspection may only be conducted against a State Organisation a maximum of two (2) times in any given week.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>A State Inspection may not be performed against a State Organisation on consecutive days (no State Inspection twice in two days).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>A State Inspection may not be scheduled at a Time that will interfere in any important duties the State Organisation has to the safety and security of the State (eg: may not be scheduled shortly before or during events like Aircraft Carrier, Bank Protection or Informant).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">e)</span>The Leader of the State Inspection may order the High Command of the State Organisation to conduct a roll-call (Code 10-1) and require all State Employees to report to their Headquarters immediately.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Where a State Employee is conducting important duties to the State (such as Processing a Suspect into the Department of Corrections) this roll-call request should be acknowledged with the reason they cannot be present given to the Leader of the State Inspection.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.1.2</span>A State Inspection may be organised and lead by any one of the following Senior Government Officials:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Governor of the State.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>A Deputy Governor of the State if the Governor has given clear instructions to conduct a State Inspection.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>The Head of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.1.3</span>The following State Organisations or Branches of the Government can assist with a State Inspection on the request of the leader of the State Inspection:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The United States Secret Service (USSS) may assist with any State Inspection.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>The Emergency Medical Services (EMS) may be requested to assist with a State Inspection.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>The Department of Justice (DOJ) may send a Lawyer to assist with the State Inspection and provide legal advice during the State Inspection.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>A Law Enforcement Organisation (FIB/LSPD/SAHP) may be requested to provide assistance with a State Inspection only if the State Inspection is within that State Organisations jurisdictional limits.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.1.4</span>No Warrant or Signed Authorisation is required for a State Inspection however a Judge may authorise specific Legal Documents on application if required for the conduct of any special duties or actions that are ordinarily outside of these Procedures for the Conduct of a State Inspection.</p>

      <h3 className="text-[17px] font-bold mt-6 mb-2 text-black dark:text-white font-merriweather"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.2</span>Rules and Procedures for the Conduct of a State Inspection.</h3>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.2.1</span>During a State Inspection, a Search of all State Property and Property that belongs to the State is permitted.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>State Property is defined as any Building or Vehicle that is the lawful Property of the State and includes the Headquarters of the State Organisation and any Additional Facilities that form part of the Headquarters or Facilities for that State Organisation (including Garages, Vehicle Yards and Depots).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>The Buildings and any Additional Facilities may be Searched to locate any State Employees who are attempting to avoid the State Inspection.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.2.2</span>During a State Inspection, a Search of any and all State Organisation Vehicles is permitted.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any State Issued Equipment, Firearms or Ammunition stored in a State Organisation Vehicle should be Investigated.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any Personal Property or Items that should not be stored in a State Organisation Vehicle should be Investigated.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.2.3</span>During a State Inspection, a Search of any and all Personal Vehicles on the Property of the State Organisation is permitted.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>Any State Employee who has stored Illegal Items or is storing Firearms or Ammunition in excess of what is permitted by the Firearms Code in their Personal Vehicle must be Arrested.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.2.4</span>During a State Inspection, an Inspection of the State Organisation and its Employees for Compliance with State Law must be performed. This includes:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>A Check of the Passport of the Employees of the State Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>A Check of the Identity of the Employees of the State Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>A Check of the Licences of the Employees of the State Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>All State Employees must have a valid Medical Insurance (as per the Labour Code)</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>All State Employees must have a valid Firearms Licence if their duties require them to carry State Issued Firearms and Ammunition (as per the Firearms Code).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">d)</span>A Search of all State Employees of the State Organisation is permitted.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Any State Employee found in possession of Illegal or Prohibited items must be Arrested.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">e)</span>A Background Check of all State Employees of the State Organisation may be conducted to determine if any Employees has a Criminal Record (ie: Previous Crimes, Prison Terms or has been Seen in Criminal Structures).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">i)</span>Any Employee who is Wanted by the State must be Arrested.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">ii)</span>Any Employee who is found to have a Criminal Record must be immediately Dismissed from the State Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-12 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">iii)</span>All Records and Documents relating to their Employment (including who Hired the Employee, their Passport and Employee’s Background Check when being Hired) must be Submitted to the Leader of the State Inspection and handed over to the Department of Labour (DOL) and the Department of Justice (DOJ) for further Investigation and further actions within the Law if necessary.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.2.5</span>During a State Inspection, an Medical Checkup for all Employees of the State Organisation may be performed by Emergency Medical Services (EMS).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>All State Employees must be in good health and free of any sickness or diseases while On-Duty.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>Any State Employee who does not have Health Insurance must purchase Health Insurance from EMS immediately.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>Any State Employee who has any illness(es) must be treated immediately by EMS.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">10.2.6</span>During or following a State Inspection the following Government Branches and Departments may conduct additional activities that are specific within their mandated Duties to the State:</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">a)</span>The Department of Justice (DOJ) may assist with a State Inspection and/or conduct an Audit of the Lawyers working for the State Organisation as well as the State Organisation’s overall compliance with State Law and the Provisions of the Charter of their State Organisation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">b)</span>The Department of Labour (DOL) may assist with a State Inspection and/or conduct an Audit of the State Organisation’s Human Resources (HR) Department for compliance with the Charter of their State Organisation, the Labour Code, hiring practices and evaluation of the State Organisation’s current workforce and training standards.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify pl-8 font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">c)</span>The Department of the Treasury (DOT) may assist with a State Inspection and conduct an Audit of the State Organisation’s Finances and Accounting.</p>

      <div className="text-center mt-12 mb-8 font-merriweather border-t border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pt-8">
        <p className="text-black dark:text-white font-bold text-[18px] uppercase tracking-wider mb-6">Signed into Legislation By</p>
        <div className="my-6">
          <p className="font-dancing text-black dark:text-white text-[32px] leading-none mb-1">Poppy Lasombra Supreme Court Judge of the State of San Andreas Minato Uchiha Governor of the State of San Andreas</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather text-center">Credit and Copyright</h2>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]">This work, and the others in this series of legislative enhancement are produced and promulgated in the interests of justice and the promotion of the legal rights of all citizens of the State of San Andreas. Final Version Amended by Supreme Court Judge Poppy Lasombra and assisted by Supreme Court Judge Mohil Yami All Articles of this new Code of Evidence and Investigation Law first written by Poppy Lasombra, Attorney General for the State of San Andreas and assisted by Judge of the State Alexandre Dubois in the 3rd Month of 2024 and building on the limited information from the Civil Code and other State Law in order to provide guidance and clarity to all Law Enforcement Officers, Judges and Lawyers in their Duties to the State. Poppy Lasombra Originally derived from work laid out by the Whitewind Law Office, Lane Stevens, and Ni Bjeebies from another city with a great history.</p>

      <h2 className="text-[20px] font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-black dark:text-white border-b border-black/20 dark:border-white/20 pb-2 font-merriweather text-center">Version History and Changes</h2>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]">First Edition Published on the 13th of March 2024. The First Edition formally moves and consolidates the limited information about Evidence and definitions of Valid and Invalid Evidence and the gathering of Evidence through Investigations and the Search of Suspects and Vehicles from Article 1.7 and Article 7 of the Code of Civil and Procedural Law and Article 15 of the Engagement Code into a new Code of Law. All other Articles and Provisions written by Poppy Lasombra where no Law existed and was determined to be necessary for the Justice System in the State of San Andreas.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added 1.3 Rules and Principles of Evidence to define general concepts and purpose of Evidence</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added and Clarified 1.4 Rules and Principles of the Use of Evidence and the Burden of Proof in an Investigation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added and Clarified 1.5 Rules and Principles for the Gathering and Recording of Evidence. Combined the scattered laws from Civil and Engagement Code to a single set of laws for the recording of evidence</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(13/03/2024)</span>1.5.3 Clarified that Recordings of mundane duties are not required but that State Employees should be ready to record if necessary.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added and Clarified 1.6 Rules and Principles for the Retaining of Evidence. Combined the scattered laws from Civil and Engagement Code to a single set of laws for the retaining of Bodycam Evidence</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added 1.7 Rules and Principles for the Chain of Custody of Evidence to help clarify the purpose of a Handover of Evidence and/or Documents. It also acts as a safeguard against Evidence that was obtained unlawfully.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added 1.8 Rules and Principles for a Request for Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added 1.8.1 Clarified that a Judge can request an officer to present evidence in Court. This is to speed up the judicial system.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added 1.8.2 Clarified the Rules for a Request for Evidence. Private Lawyers were being blocked from access to essential evidence for them to perform their duties to their Clients</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added 1.8.3 Clarified that a High Command (such as IA) has the right to ask for Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added and Clarified 1.9 provisions for Anonymous Evidence to protect whistleblowers from unlawful treatment within their State Organisations and to protect the identity of witnesses during a Case or Trial. Clarified provisions for Anonymous or Confidential Evidence and how this can be used in a Trial (in camera)</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Clarified 1.10 Rules and Principles of Classified Evidence. Clarified the provisions of Classified Evidence and how this can be used and who may or may not be excluded from access to Classified Evidence</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Moved 1.11 Rules and Principles of a State’s Witness from the Criminal Code to the Evidence Code as it also applies to non-criminal cases.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(12/03/2024)</span>Clarified that the Evidence may be protected as Anonymous Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(12/03/2024)</span>Clarified that the Evidence may be protected as Classified Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Added 1.12 Rules and Principles for the Duration of Validity for Video and Photo Evidence. Clarified provisions for what should be done to prevent Evidence from Expiring and how the Court can resolve these situations where Suspects or Lawyers attempt to delay a Case or Hearing.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(11/03/2024)</span>Clarified 1.12 Rules and Principles for the Duration of Validity for Video and Photo Evidence. No change in duration of 7-days however some further safeguards as to Suspects that intentionally cause delays to force expired evidence were added.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added Article 2 for Definitions within Evidence Law.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.1 Definition of an Investigation as per the Existing Civil Code.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.2 Definition of Reasonable Suspicion. Fundamental principle in law for Detention and Stop and Frisk (Terry Stops) but was never defined.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.3 Definition of Probable Cause. Fundamental principle in law for Detention, Arrest and Searches but was never defined.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.4 Definition of a Witness.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.5 Definition of Admissible Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.6 Definition of Valid Evidence. Clear definition of what is Valid Evidence</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.7 Definition of Invalid Evidence. Clear definition of what is Invalid Evidence and that invalid evidence cannot be used under the Exclusion Rule of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.8 Definition of Inadmissible Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.9 Definition of Illegal Evidence. Clear definition of what is Illegal Evidence and that Illegal Evidence is also Inadmissible Evidence (ie cannot be used under the Exclusion Rule of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.10 Definition of Supporting Evidence. Clear definition of Supporting Evidence that does not prove the facts directly but is used to make supporting arguments in Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 2.11 Clear Definition of Excluded Evidence and the Exclusion Rule in Law.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Clear definition of what is Inadmissible Evidence and that Inadmissible Evidence cannot be used under the Exclusion Rule of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Defined the Concept of the Fruit of the Poisoned Tree that Illegal Evidence may make all other Evidence that is based on the Illegal Evidence also illegal and inadmissible.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added Article 3 as the Standards of Evidence. A general set of terminology and common standards for the use of Evidence for the Court to make a ruling or grant additional documentation in an Investigation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.1 Rules and Principles of the Standards of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.2 Standard of No Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.3 Standard of Insufficient Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.4 Standard of Circumstantial Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.5 Standard of Prima Facie Evidence. Clarified that Prima Facie is the lowest form of valid evidence for further investigation.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.6 Standard of Preponderance of the Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.7 Standard of Clear and Convincing Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 3.8 Standard of Evidence Beyond a Reasonable Doubt.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.1 Forms of Valid and Admissible Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.2 Bodycam Evidence for State Employees. Clarified the general rules for Bodycam and Proof of Bodycam.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.3 Bodycam Evidence for Citizens. Clarified the general rules for Bodycam and Proof of Bodycam when being used by a Civilian.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(19/03/2024)</span>4.3.1 a) ii) Fixed numbering issue and reference to 4.2</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.4 Document and Records Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.5 Photographic (Photo) Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.6 Search Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.7 Crime Scene Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.8 Ballistics Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.9 Eye-Witness Testimony and Testimony Under Oath. Full clarifications of Affidavits and Depositions as well as Direct and Cross Examination in Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.10 Statements and Questioning of a Suspect (requirements of the Miranda Rights as per the US Law regarding questioning of a Suspect under Detention).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.11 Organisation Internal Log (Leaderboard) Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.12 PDA Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.13 Organisation eMail.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.14 GPS Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.15 VIN Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.16 Phone Evidence (Calls and Messages).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.16.1 Phone Calls</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.16.2 Phone Messages</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 4.17 Radio Communications.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Added 4.18 Identification of a Citizen, State Employee or Suspect. A single clear rule that was usable and took into account problems with masks and recognising another Citizen was needed.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Clarified 5.1 Forms of Invalid and Inadmissible Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Clarified 5.2 Corrupted Evidence. This existed as part of Article 1.7 of the Civil Code but is added here for Clarification of Rules of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Clarified 5.3 Manipulated Evidence. This existed as part of Article 1.7 of the Civil Code but is added here for Clarification of Rules of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Clarified 5.4 Incomplete Evidence. This existed as part of Article 1.7 of the Civil Code but is added here for Clarification of Rules of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Clarified 5.5 Missing Evidence. This existed as part of Article 1.7 of the Civil Code but is added here for Clarification of Rules of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Clarified 5.6 Unreliable Testimony. This existed as part of Article 1.7 of the Civil Code but is added here for Clarification of Rules of Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 5.7 Private eMail. Clarified that Private eMail cannot be used as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 5.8 Second Hand Recordings. Clarified that recordings through eMail (or other similar sources) cannot be used as Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 6.1 Forms of Illegal Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 6.2 Illegal Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 6.3 Fabricated Evidence.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 6.4 Violation(s) of Attorney Client Privilege.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 6.5 Violation(s) of Privacy.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 7.1 Rules and Principles for a Lawful Search of a Suspect or Citizen. Previously these formed part of the Civil Code Article 7. Other Grounds for a Search existed in other Codes of the Law (such as an Unwilling Participant in the Criminal Code) or were clearly implied in the Law. All Grounds for a Valid Search of a Citizen or Suspect have been gathered here in a single point of reference.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added Rules for this Search Evidence and where it may be considered inadmissible if the Grounds for the Search do not apply.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 8.1 Rules and Principles for a Lawful Search of a Private Property or Residence. Previously these formed part of the Civil Code Article 7.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 9.1 Rules and Principles for a Lawful Search of a Private Vehicle. Previously these formed part of the Civil Code Article 7. Other Grounds for a Search existed in other Codes of the Law (Traffic Code) such as an or were clearly implied in the Law. All Grounds for a Valid Search of a Vehicle have been gathered here in a single point of reference.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 9.2 Rules and Principles for Confiscation of Illegal Items from a Vehicle. Clarified the Provisions and requirements for Confiscation from a Vehicle (trunk must logically be open).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added Article 10. Laws and Procedures for a State Inspection. Almost no proper laws or procedures and guidelines for a State Inspection existed and State Inspections were only briefly mentioned in Article 7 of the Civil Code. This Article has been written and added as part of this Code as a State Inspection is a formal Investigation into a State Organisation by the Government and thus should form part of the Evidence and Investigation Code.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 10.1 Clarified the regulations for a State Inspection. No clear guidelines or laws for when and how a State Inspection can be conducted existed in the law and what still exists in Civil Code Article 7 is completely inadequate.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(03/03/2024)</span>Added 10.2 Procedures for a State Inspection. No clear guidelines or laws for what was permitted during a State Inspection existed in the law. Additional Amendments and Recommendations to First Edition Published on the 24th of June 2024</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(19/03/2024)</span>Added 10.2.4 e) Added that a BGC on the Organisation Employees is permitted. This should be done outside of the State Inspection as well but may also be done during Inspection. Further clarified the actions that must be taken in the event of an Employee having a Criminal Record.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(19/03/2024)</span>Clarified 4.4 that Charters, Laws etc must be Signed in order to be Valid as they are definitely official documents.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Clarified 4.4 Added Official Registries and Government Records to evidence that does not expire.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Fixed small errors, numbering and empty sub-clauses</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Clarification of 4.2.1 a) Refers to a Proof of Bodycam (turns on Bodycam) this is valid regardless of an Officer being sent to the hospital (the DOJ cannot reasonably check 4 hours of bodycam to find a reason to make it invalid).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>4.2.1 a) v) Added and Clarified that a Change in Clothing or Uniform does invalidate a Proof of Bodycam (the bodycam is logically attached to the outside of the clothing)</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>4.2.1 a) vii) Added and Clarified that it is only the Evidence (the Recording) that cannot be used (the Proof of Bodycam still remains valid as per above)</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>4.2.1 b) iii) Clarified that a Refresh or Restart of Bodycam has no requirement to be done at the start of a recording. This is logically impossible with many methods of clipping or saving of bodycam recordings.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Fixed Numbering of types of Evidence from 4.8 onwards.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Added 9.1.1 a) The Law Enforcement Officer must retain valid Evidence of the reason for the Search and the conduct of the Search for a minimum of 48-hours.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Added 9.1.1 b) The Law Enforcement Officers must be able to prove they had access to the trunk to Search.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Added 9.2.1 b) The Law Enforcement Officers must be able to prove they had access to the trunk to confiscate.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Added 9.2.1 c) Added the clear definition of an unlawful Search and Seizure.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Amended 10.1.3 Set limitations to assistance by LEO&apos;s based on jurisdictional limits.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Amended 10.1.2. The Deputy Governor should receive clear instructions to conduct the State Inspection in the Governors absence or unavailability.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Amended 10.1.2 and 10.2.6. The Attorney General has clear duties during a State Inspection and should assist where necessary but not should lead a State Inspection or handle Internal Affairs audits. Those will be the duties of DHS. Additional Amendments to First Edition Published on the 18th of July 2024</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Added 10.1.1 d) A State Inspection must not interfere with the State Organisations duties to the State (at the time of adding, a FIB Inspection was done shortly before informant which caused major issues).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Clarified 4.9 Testimony (Verbal and Written) with clear rules and provisions. Previously this was vague and lacked clear rules for the taking of Written and Verbal Evidence as well as questioning of Witnesses in Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(04/04/2024)</span>Added 4.2.2 for the requirements for Raid Warrant Bodycam and Evidence by FIB due to clarification as to the requirements.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Clarified 4.10 For Statements and Questioning after Detention and/or Arrest. As per the origins of the Miranda Rights under US Law this is why all Suspect must be read the Miranda Rights.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Clarified 4.11.1 that this also includes Promotions and Dismissal of an Employee.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Clarified further that a Proof of Bodycam and the Recording are separate considerations for being valid (eg: The Proof of Bodycam remains valid and is not invalidated by being sent to the hospital and it is only the Bodycam Recording itself that is made invalid).</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(18/07/2024)</span>Clarified 7.1.2 b) and c) Clarified the Principles and Grounds for Reasonable Suspicion and Probable Cause using the generally accepted definition by the US Supreme Court.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(24/03/2024)</span>Added and Clarified 4.2.1 a) iii) A Refresh of a Bodycam is not required following a Code A or other such interruption and is only required following a formal saving of the bodycam recording.</p>
      <p className="mb-3 text-justify font-merriweather leading-relaxed text-[#5c6470] dark:text-[#9aa1b0]"><span className="font-bold text-black dark:text-white mr-2">(18/07/2024)</span>Clarified 2.8 Definition of the Exclusion Rule of Evidence. Moved each of the separate concepts for Excluded Evidence to a single provision for ease of reading and understanding.</p>
    </div>
  );
}